From a19370ee225232700a3b5213ef2443b730dc4310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:58:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(process): add the yellow needs-maintainer review
 label

A "Not built - needs a maintainer look" review (a new dependency, or a
build.rs / scripts / .github change the reviewer reads and does not build)
had no label of its own, so such a PR looked unreviewed on the PR list.
The review-prs skill's label table, the PR-reviewer verdict line, the
README contributing table and AGENTS.md's review-label sentence now name
needs-maintainer (yellow): reviewed with no blockers, waiting for the
owner's decision.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md      |  4 +++-
 .claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md | 11 ++++++++++-
 AGENTS.md                          |  4 +++-
 README.md                          |  1 +
 4 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md b/.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md
index 9892f74f..42a0358b 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md
@@ -85,7 +85,9 @@ merge.
 6. **Post the review** (comment only) with this shape, plain and specific,
    first line `<!-- pr-reviewer: <headRefOid> -->`:
    - one-line verdict: "Ready for the maintainer to merge" / "Needs changes
-     before merge" / "Not built - needs a maintainer look";
+     before merge" / "Not built - needs a maintainer look" (the last, with
+     no blockers, gets the yellow `needs-maintainer` label - see the
+     review-prs skill, step 2b);
    - What looks good (short bullets);
    - Local results merged with main (build, each suite with pass counts,
      clippy) - exact failure text in a code block;
diff --git a/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
index c95a3811..895f1a60 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
@@ -92,12 +92,21 @@ we can find em"):
 | `merge-ready` | green | review clean AND merges cleanly with main - the owner can merge now |
 | `needs-rework` | red | the review found blocking items |
 | `conflicts` | orange | conflicts with main - needs a branch refresh (`git merge origin/main`) |
+| `needs-maintainer` | yellow | reviewed, no blockers, but the owner must decide first: a new dependency, or a `build.rs` / scripts / `.github` change the reviewer reads and does not build ("Not built - needs a maintainer look") |
+
+`needs-maintainer` (user, 2026-11-09: "that needs-maintainer needs to
+into the skill right?") gives the "Not built - needs a maintainer look"
+verdict a label. Without it such a PR carried none and looked unreviewed
+on the PR list. The owner removes it after deciding: on a yes it becomes
+`merge-ready`, or is built and reviewed in full first; on a no it is
+closed or gets `needs-rework`.
 
 After posting the review, read `gh pr view <N> --json mergeable`
 (re-read once if it says `UNKNOWN`):
 - clean review + `MERGEABLE` -> add `merge-ready`, remove `needs-rework` and `conflicts`;
 - clean review + `CONFLICTING` -> add `conflicts`, remove `merge-ready` (never green while it conflicts);
-- blocking review -> add `needs-rework`, remove `merge-ready`; also add `conflicts` if it conflicts.
+- blocking review -> add `needs-rework`, remove `merge-ready`; also add `conflicts` if it conflicts;
+- "Not built - needs a maintainer look" with no blockers -> add `needs-maintainer`, remove `merge-ready`; also add `conflicts` if it conflicts. With blockers it is `needs-rework` as above, and the comment still names the owner's decision.
 
 A red or orange verdict also turns the PR back into a draft
 (`gh pr ready <N> --undo`): the author fixes it there, pushes, and flags it
diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 4c6b7a0a..a701c12d 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -605,7 +605,9 @@ PR*s made by owner should be reviewd and tagged"); a fix PR merges once
 that review is clean, a `feat` or breaking PR at the cut (step 1 above).
 **Review labels**, one colour per state: green `merge-ready` (clean review
 and mergeable), red `needs-rework` (blockers), orange `conflicts` (no
-longer merges with `main`). On red or orange the reviewer turns one of our
+longer merges with `main`), yellow `needs-maintainer` (no blockers, but
+read, not built: a new dependency or a `build.rs` / scripts / `.github`
+change waits for the owner's decision). On red or orange the reviewer turns one of our
 own PRs back into a draft; a fork PR is left as its contributor set it,
 and the review comment says what to fix.
 
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6f0eb4ab..f8929a39 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -294,6 +294,7 @@ re-tested, and only then is flagged ready again.
 | `merge-ready` (green) | clean review and mergeable | waits for the maintainer's merge |
 | `needs-rework` (red) | review found blockers | a maintainer PR goes back to draft; fix, push, flag ready again (a fork PR stays as its contributor set it; the review comment says what to fix) |
 | `conflicts` (orange) | no longer merges with `main` | a maintainer PR goes back to draft; merge `main`, re-test, flag ready again (a fork PR: the contributor merges `main`) |
+| `needs-maintainer` (yellow) | reviewed with no blockers, but it adds a dependency or changes `build.rs`, scripts or `.github`, so it was read, not built | waits for the maintainer's decision |
 
 When a PR comes back from draft with a new head, that head gets a fresh
 review; the marker `<!-- pr-reviewer: <head sha> -->` in the review comment

From de8cedf1bda63967c948a09724e3384da757f4e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
